      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "MiniMax-H3_R2I Turbo",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MiniMax-H3_R2I Turbo\n\nThis workflow keeps the model-specific reference conditioning from `MiniMax H3 Reference to Video`, but intentionally ignores that node's video latent. Sampling uses the regular one-frame `Empty Latent Image` path added by ComfyUI PR 15677.\n\n- Turbo LoRA: `minimax_h3_turbo_v4_step600_ema_pruned_comfyui.safetensors`\n- LoRA strength: 1.0\n- Sampling: 8 steps / `euler` / `beta`\n- Decode/reference VAE: `minimax_h3_t1_image_vae_step1597.safetensors` (single-image only)\n- Audio VAE: connected because `MiniMax H3 Reference to Video` declares `audio_vae` as a required input. It is not encoded or decoded when only reference images are connected.\n- Reference tags: `<Picture 1>`, `<Picture 2>`\n- Output: one PNG\n\nEnter exact pixel dimensions in Width and Height. Both values must be multiples of 32. Useful presets:\n\n| Ratio | 1K | 2K |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| 16:9 | 1024×576 | 2048×1152 |\n| 9:16 | 576×1024 | 1152×2048 |\n| 4:3 | 1024×768 | 2048×1536 |\n| 3:4 | 768×1024 | 1536×2048 |\n| 1:1 | 1024×1024 | 2048×2048 |\n\nThe `length=5` value belongs only to the unused conditioning node latent; it does not cause five target frames to be sampled. Do not use this image VAE for multi-frame video workflows."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## MiniMax-H3_R2I Turbo\n\nThis workflow keeps the model-specific reference conditioning from `MiniMax H3 Reference to Video`, but intentionally ignores that node's video latent. Sampling uses the regular one-frame `Empty Latent Image` path added by ComfyUI PR 15677.\n\n- Turbo LoRA: `minimax_h3_turbo_v4_step600_ema_pruned_comfyui.safetensors`\n- LoRA strength: 1.0\n- Sampling: 8 steps / `euler` / `beta`\n- Decode/reference VAE: `minimax_h3_t1_image_vae_step1597.safetensors` (single-image only)\n- Audio VAE: connected because `MiniMax H3 Reference to Video` declares `audio_vae` as a required input. It is not encoded or decoded when only reference images are connected.\n- Reference tags: `<Picture 1>`, `<Picture 2>`\n- Output: one PNG\n\nEnter exact pixel dimensions in Width and Height. Both values must be multiples of 32. Useful presets:\n\n| Ratio | 1K | 2K |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| 16:9 | 1024×576 | 2048×1152 |\n| 9:16 | 576×1024 | 1152×2048 |\n| 4:3 | 1024×768 | 2048×1536 |\n| 3:4 | 768×1024 | 1536×2048 |\n| 1:1 | 1024×1024 | 2048×2048 |\n\nThe `length=5` value belongs only to the unused conditioning node latent; it does not cause five target frames to be sampled. Do not use this image VAE for multi-frame video workflows."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
